---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const schema = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "ProfessionalService",
  "name": "Alturascope",
  "description": "Reality capture, 3D documentation, and conditions surveys for construction teams and specialist clients across the US, Canada, and the UK.",
  "url": "https://alturascope.com/",
  "areaServed": ["United States", "Canada", "United Kingdom"],
  "serviceType": "Reality Capture and Site Documentation",
  "sameAs": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/111948383"]
});
---
<Layout
  title="About Alturascope | Site Documentation & Estimating"
  description="Built by construction people tired of expensive decisions made on bad site information. 500+ sites documented, and an estimating desk with 33 years behind it."
  canonical="https://alturascope.com/about/"
  schema={schema}
  fullWidth={true}
>
  <div data-hero-page>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="relative h-[50vh] min-h-[350px] flex items-center justify-center">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-navy">
        <img
          src="/Images/site-interior-1.jpg"
          width="1600"
          height="1205"
          alt="Aerial orthographic survey of a commercial building roof, showing plant, membrane condition and the surrounding site"
          class="w-full h-full object-cover opacity-30"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[rgba(11,31,58,0.72)]"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="relative z-10 text-center px-6 max-w-[800px] mx-auto">
        <h1 class="text-[2rem] md:text-[2.8rem] font-light text-offwhite leading-tight">
          Built on the understanding that accurate documentation changes outcomes.
        </h1>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The Company -->
    <section class="bg-white section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-[760px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="space-y-5 text-midgrey leading-body text-[1.05rem]">
          <p>
            Alturascope exists because the documentation most project teams receive doesn't match the decisions they're trying to make. Survey reports with no useful structure. Digital twins delivered without context. Conditions information that arrives too late, or in a format nobody can actually use.
          </p>
          <p>
            We built something different. Every Alturascope visit produces the same structured deliverable architecture — not because we're rigid, but because consistency is what allows project teams to compare sites, brief consultants, and move forward with confidence. The brief changes. The standard doesn't.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our background is in construction and the built environment — nearly two decades of it, across commercial fit-out, conservation, and project delivery at every scale. That experience includes hands-on construction work, collaboration with architects and conservation specialists on some of Britain's most significant historic buildings, and documentation work across almost every US state and every Canadian province. We know what buildings look like from the inside — not just through a camera.
          </p>
          <p>
            We are based in Montreal and operate a national travel model across the US and Canada, with a dedicated UK operation for work in Britain. We take on a relatively small number of projects at any time, which means every one gets the same attention.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Who you are dealing with -->
    <section class="bg-offwhite section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-[1000px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,300px)_1fr] gap-10 md:gap-14 items-start">
          <figure class="m-0">
            <img
              src="/Images/aph-image.jpg"
              alt="Andrew Harris, founder of Alturascope"
              width="1150"
              height="1533"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
              class="w-full h-auto"
            />
          </figure>
          <div>
            <p class="label text-gold mb-4">Who You Are Dealing With</p>
            <h2 class="text-[1.8rem] md:text-[2rem] font-light text-navy leading-tight">
              Andrew Harris
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-midgrey text-[0.95rem]">Founder &mdash; Alturascope</p>
            <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-midgrey leading-body">
              <p>
                Eighteen years in construction and the built environment, across commercial
                fit-out, conservation and project delivery. Before Alturascope that meant
                hands-on work on site, and collaboration with architects and conservation
                specialists on some of Britain&rsquo;s most significant historic buildings.
              </p>
              <p>
                Since then, documentation work across almost every US state and every Canadian
                province &mdash; several hundred commercial sites, most of them retail and office
                units being handed over, stripped out or fitted for their next occupier.
              </p>
              <p>
                It is a small operation by design. When you send a building or a bid package,
                it is dealt with by someone who has stood in that kind of space with a tape in
                their hand, not routed to a queue.
              </p>
              <p>
                <a href="/work/locations/" class="text-navy font-medium hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity">See a sample of the buildings &rarr;</a>
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The Estimating Desk -->
    <section class="bg-white section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-[760px] mx-auto px-6">
        <p class="label text-gold mb-4">The Estimating Desk</p>
        <h2 class="text-[1.8rem] md:text-[2rem] font-light text-navy leading-tight">
          Thirty-three years, and a machine that checks the work.
        </h2>
        <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-midgrey leading-body">
          <p>
            In 2026 we added a second service: <a href="/estimating/" class="text-navy font-medium hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity">construction estimating</a>. Contractors send us a bid package and we send back a priced, white-labeled quote under their own name, usually inside two working days.
          </p>
          <p>
            It came out of the same observation the survey business came out of. Documentation answers &ldquo;what am I working with?&rdquo; The very next question anybody asks is &ldquo;what will it cost?&rdquo; &mdash; and the two are far better answered together, because renovation estimates go wrong in the gap between what the drawing says and what the building actually is.
          </p>
          <p>
            The desk brings together eighteen years in construction and, in Selwyn Doling, fifteen years in professional estimating, working inside a contractor operations platform that handles the take-off, the rate library and the document generation &mdash; and that refuses to release an estimate carrying a quantity with no source or an exclusion with no stated reason. Every pack is reviewed and signed off by a career estimator before it is issued, and it is issued to the client as a draft for them to release under their own name.
          </p>
          <p>
            We do not contract, we do not supply materials, and we do not take a percentage of the job &mdash; so we have no reason to want a number to be anything other than right. And we will not price work on a site we have documented for the other side of the table.
          </p>
          <p>
            <a href="/estimating/" class="text-navy font-medium hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity">See how the estimating desk works &rarr;</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What sets us apart -->
    <section class="bg-offwhite section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-[760px] mx-auto px-6">
        <p class="label text-gold mb-10">What Sets Us Apart</p>

        <div class="space-y-10">
          <div>
            <p class="text-navy font-medium mb-2">We built ScopeWalk because email folders aren't good enough.</p>
            <p class="text-midgrey leading-body">
              Every deliverable lives in a structured, permanent portal — not a WeTransfer link. Your team can access every project at any time. For multi-site programmes, you can compare any two properties side by side.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-navy font-medium mb-2">We include travel. Always.</p>
            <p class="text-midgrey leading-body">
              Nationwide coverage means nothing if travel costs arrive as a surprise. Our pricing includes travel to any location in the US, Canada, or the UK. You brief us once. We handle the logistics.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-navy font-medium mb-2">We scope before we quote.</p>
            <p class="text-midgrey leading-body">
              Every project starts with a conversation about what you're trying to decide. That shapes what we capture, which shapes what you receive. We don't send a standard package when a tailored brief would serve you better.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="bg-white section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-[600px] mx-auto px-6 text-center">
        <p class="text-midgrey leading-body text-lg">
          If you have a project — straightforward or otherwise — we'd like to hear about it.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="btn-primary mt-8">Get In Touch</a>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-6 text-sm">
          <a href="/" class="text-navy font-medium hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity">Home &rarr;</a>
          <a href="/services/" class="text-navy font-medium hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity">Our services &rarr;</a>
          <a href="/work/" class="text-navy font-medium hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity">The Standard &rarr;</a>
          <a href="/services/construction-documentation/" class="text-navy font-medium hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity">Construction documentation &rarr;</a>
          <a href="/estimating/" class="text-navy font-medium hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity">Estimating desk &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>
</Layout>
